WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.221 --> 00:00:01.447
- Good morning Believe Nation.

00:00:01.447 --> 00:00:05.130
Today's message is be
honest with yourself.

00:00:05.130 --> 00:00:06.761
Over to you Mel Robins.

00:00:06.761 --> 00:00:09.108
(cock crowing)

00:00:09.108 --> 00:00:11.808
♫ I wake up every morning

00:00:11.808 --> 00:00:14.650
♫ Espresso keep me going

00:00:14.650 --> 00:00:18.498
♫ I wake up every morning

00:00:18.498 --> 00:00:22.278
- We live in the most
amazing moment in time.

00:00:22.278 --> 00:00:24.554
So that thing that you have up here.

00:00:24.554 --> 00:00:27.320
Whatever it may be, you
want to use healthy eating

00:00:27.320 --> 00:00:29.288
to cure your diabetes.

00:00:29.288 --> 00:00:32.002
You want to figure out how to take care

00:00:32.002 --> 00:00:35.038
of the elders and start
a new hospice center.

00:00:35.038 --> 00:00:37.668
You want to move to
Africa and build a school.

00:00:37.668 --> 00:00:38.683
Guess what?

00:00:38.683 --> 00:00:41.837
You can walk into a bookstore right now.

00:00:41.837 --> 00:00:45.251
And buy at least ten books
written by credentialed experts

00:00:45.251 --> 00:00:47.438
on how the hell you do it.

00:00:47.438 --> 00:00:48.995
You could google it.

00:00:48.995 --> 00:00:52.053
And you could probably find
at least, I don't know,

00:00:52.053 --> 00:00:56.837
a thousand blogs documenting
the step by step by step

00:00:56.837 --> 00:01:00.694
transformation that somebody
else is already doing.

00:01:00.694 --> 00:01:04.777
You can find anybody online
and cyber stalk them.

00:01:06.456 --> 00:01:08.567
You can just walk in their footsteps and

00:01:08.567 --> 00:01:10.857
just use signs of drafting.

00:01:10.857 --> 00:01:12.112
Follow what everyone else has done

00:01:12.112 --> 00:01:14.806
because somebody else is already doing it.

00:01:14.806 --> 00:01:18.061
So why don't you have what you want

00:01:18.061 --> 00:01:20.570
when you have all the
information that you need.

00:01:20.570 --> 00:01:22.608
You have the context that you need.

00:01:22.608 --> 00:01:24.870
There are probably free tools online

00:01:24.870 --> 00:01:27.549
that allow you to start a
business or join a group or

00:01:27.549 --> 00:01:30.049
do whatever the heck you want.

00:01:31.550 --> 00:01:34.050
It all comes down to one word.

00:01:39.034 --> 00:01:41.440
Shut the front door, you
know what I'm talking about?

00:01:41.440 --> 00:01:43.405
(laughter)

00:01:43.405 --> 00:01:44.763
The F bomb.

00:01:44.763 --> 00:01:46.096
It's everywhere.

00:01:47.572 --> 00:01:48.616
You hear it all the time.

00:01:48.616 --> 00:01:51.098
And I honestly don't
understand what the appeal is

00:01:51.098 --> 00:01:52.263
of the word.

00:01:52.263 --> 00:01:55.634
I mean you don't sound
smart when you say it.

00:01:55.634 --> 00:01:59.801
And it's really not expressing
how you really feel.

00:02:00.944 --> 00:02:04.422
It's sort of a cheap,
you know, shot to take.

00:02:04.422 --> 00:02:08.319
And of course, you know,
I'm talking about the word

00:02:08.319 --> 00:02:09.152
Fine.

00:02:10.289 --> 00:02:11.215
How you doing?

00:02:11.215 --> 00:02:12.215
Oh I'm fine.

00:02:13.467 --> 00:02:15.217
Oh really, you are?

00:02:15.217 --> 00:02:18.381
Dragging around those extra
40 pounds, you're fine?

00:02:18.381 --> 00:02:21.620
Feeling like roommates with
your spouse, you're fine?

00:02:21.620 --> 00:02:24.534
You haven't had sex in
four months, you're fine?

00:02:24.534 --> 00:02:25.367
Really?

00:02:27.430 --> 00:02:29.679
I don't think so.

00:02:29.679 --> 00:02:33.119
But see here's the deal with
saying that you're fine.

00:02:33.119 --> 00:02:35.559
It's actually genius.

00:02:35.559 --> 00:02:38.079
Because if you're fine, you
don't have to do anything

00:02:38.079 --> 00:02:38.912
about it.

00:02:40.432 --> 00:02:43.242
But when you think about this word fine,

00:02:43.242 --> 00:02:45.460
it just makes me so angry.

00:02:45.460 --> 00:02:47.418
I mean here we are at a
conference about being alive and

00:02:47.418 --> 00:02:51.585
you're going to describe the
experience of being alive as fine?

00:02:52.829 --> 00:02:55.329
What a flimsy and feeble word.

00:02:56.349 --> 00:02:57.697
You're crappy, say you're crappy.

00:02:57.697 --> 00:03:00.174
If you're amazing, say you're amazing.

00:03:00.174 --> 00:03:02.087
Tell the truth.

00:03:02.087 --> 00:03:05.117
And this not only goes
for the social construct.

00:03:05.117 --> 00:03:06.504
Oh I don't want to burden
you with the fact that

00:03:06.504 --> 00:03:08.396
I hate my life or hey I'm amazing,

00:03:08.396 --> 00:03:10.053
but that would make you feel terrible.

00:03:10.053 --> 00:03:11.002
(laughter)

00:03:11.002 --> 00:03:12.765
The bigger issue

00:03:12.765 --> 00:03:16.932
the bigger issue with fine is
that you say it to yourself.

00:03:18.301 --> 00:03:21.189
That thing that you want, I guarantee you

00:03:21.189 --> 00:03:23.664
you've convinced yourself that you're fine

00:03:23.664 --> 00:03:24.831
not having it.

00:03:27.159 --> 00:03:29.531
That's why you're not pushing yourself.

00:03:29.531 --> 00:03:32.286
It's the areas in your
life where you've given up.

00:03:32.286 --> 00:03:34.014
Or you've said oh I'm fine.

00:03:34.014 --> 00:03:36.191
My mom's never going to
change so I just can't

00:03:36.191 --> 00:03:37.867
have that conversation.

00:03:37.867 --> 00:03:39.710
I'm fine, you know, we
got to wait until the kids

00:03:39.710 --> 00:03:41.927
graduate before we get
divorced so, we'll just

00:03:41.927 --> 00:03:44.346
sleep in separate bedrooms.

00:03:44.346 --> 00:03:47.617
I'm fine, I lost job, I
can barely pay my bills

00:03:47.617 --> 00:03:50.700
but whatever, it's hard to get a job.

00:03:51.790 --> 00:03:55.254
And you know, one of the
reasons why this word also

00:03:55.254 --> 00:03:57.337
just annoys me so much is

00:03:58.932 --> 00:04:01.267
scientists have calculated,

00:04:01.267 --> 00:04:03.445
oh yeah, I'm coming down,

00:04:03.445 --> 00:04:06.557
scientists have calculated
(laughter and clapping)

00:04:06.557 --> 00:04:08.807
the odds of you being born.

00:04:13.267 --> 00:04:15.373
That's right, they crunched the numbers.

00:04:15.373 --> 00:04:16.956
I see you up there.

00:04:17.970 --> 00:04:19.844
They have crunched the numbers on you,

00:04:19.844 --> 00:04:22.582
I know you guys standing up,
you want to sit down for this.

00:04:22.582 --> 00:04:25.764
They've crunched the numbers
on you being born and

00:04:25.764 --> 00:04:27.642
they took into account

00:04:27.642 --> 00:04:31.392
all of the wars and the
natural disasters and

00:04:32.648 --> 00:04:36.060
the dinosaurs and everything else.

00:04:36.060 --> 00:04:38.727
And do you realize that the odds

00:04:40.570 --> 00:04:43.275
the odds of you, yeah right
here, put your computer away,

00:04:43.275 --> 00:04:44.120
stand up for me.

00:04:44.120 --> 00:04:46.870
Doug. (laughter)

00:04:47.898 --> 00:04:49.794
So the odds of Doug here, turn around

00:04:49.794 --> 00:04:51.282
say hi to every body.

00:04:51.282 --> 00:04:54.032
The odds of Doug, Doug being born

00:04:55.589 --> 00:04:58.454
at the moment in time he was born

00:04:58.454 --> 00:05:00.416
to the parents you were born to

00:05:00.416 --> 00:05:04.245
with the DNA structure that you have

00:05:04.245 --> 00:05:06.662
one in four hundred trillion.

00:05:09.666 --> 00:05:11.548
Isn't that amazing?
- [Doug] I'm so lucky.

00:05:11.548 --> 00:05:13.470
- [Mel] Yes. (laughter)

00:05:13.470 --> 00:05:16.028
You're not fine, you're fantastic.

00:05:16.028 --> 00:05:20.036
You have life changing ideas for a reason.

00:05:20.036 --> 00:05:23.162
And it's not to torture yourself.

00:05:23.162 --> 00:05:26.468
Thank you, thank you Doug. (applause)

00:05:26.468 --> 00:05:28.061
You know Christine was right

00:05:28.061 --> 00:05:30.937
when she said all of
you could be on stage.

00:05:30.937 --> 00:05:33.602
Because all of you, we're
all in this category.

00:05:33.602 --> 00:05:36.102
One and four hundred trillion.

00:05:38.352 --> 00:05:40.784
All day long, you have ideas

00:05:40.784 --> 00:05:42.681
that could change your life,

00:05:42.681 --> 00:05:43.946
that could change the world,

00:05:43.946 --> 00:05:46.325
that could change the way that you feel.

00:05:46.325 --> 00:05:48.246
And what do you do with them?

00:05:48.246 --> 00:05:49.546
Nothing.

00:05:49.546 --> 00:05:53.256
Oh, hopefully I won't moon you. (laughter)

00:05:53.256 --> 00:05:54.451
You didn't pay for that.

00:05:54.451 --> 00:05:55.509
- To be a successful entrepreneur

00:05:55.509 --> 00:05:58.054
you need to be allergic to mediocrity.

00:05:58.054 --> 00:06:00.635
You need to have an allergy to mediocrity.

00:06:00.635 --> 00:06:03.357
You got to take something
that has been good and

00:06:03.357 --> 00:06:05.050
has been good and has been good and

00:06:05.050 --> 00:06:05.883
make it great.

00:06:05.883 --> 00:06:07.442
Be upset at good.

00:06:07.442 --> 00:06:09.091
That's the way great progress happens.

00:06:09.091 --> 00:06:10.891
And the only way you do
it is because you have

00:06:10.891 --> 00:06:12.360
that deep love for what you're doing.

00:06:12.360 --> 00:06:13.865
You have the deep love for your business

00:06:13.865 --> 00:06:15.581
because otherwise, you're
going to say, that okay,

00:06:15.581 --> 00:06:17.060
you know what, that video I made,

00:06:17.060 --> 00:06:18.548
that was okay, I'm good with it.

00:06:18.548 --> 00:06:20.631
And you just keep staying
on the same treadmill

00:06:20.631 --> 00:06:22.102
instead of moving forward.

00:06:22.102 --> 00:06:24.242
I recently got a comment on
one of my Youtube videos.

00:06:24.242 --> 00:06:25.660
I was talking about my book.

00:06:25.660 --> 00:06:27.412
And I'm not super happy
with my book cover,

00:06:27.412 --> 00:06:29.432
I was talking about lessons I had learned

00:06:29.432 --> 00:06:32.061
in my book launch and one
of the things that I wish

00:06:32.061 --> 00:06:33.978
that I had more time on
was my book cover because

00:06:33.978 --> 00:06:35.484
I wasn't a huge fan of it.

00:06:35.484 --> 00:06:36.648
And I got a comment.

00:06:36.648 --> 00:06:39.863
And the comment was, it's
easily an above-average

00:06:39.863 --> 00:06:40.987
book cover.

00:06:40.987 --> 00:06:41.820
And I get it.

00:06:41.820 --> 00:06:42.653
I get the love.

00:06:42.653 --> 00:06:43.712
I don't want to rip into this comment.

00:06:43.712 --> 00:06:44.651
I get the love, right.

00:06:44.651 --> 00:06:46.258
It's what we do.

00:06:46.258 --> 00:06:47.779
We try to encourage others to do better.

00:06:47.779 --> 00:06:51.418
When we have found that we
are unhappy with something,

00:06:51.418 --> 00:06:54.000
right, and we're down,
what do people tell us?

00:06:54.000 --> 00:06:56.045
Oh, you're doing a great job,
you're doing really well,

00:06:56.045 --> 00:06:57.711
it's an above average performance.

00:06:57.711 --> 00:06:59.750
I don't want to be above average.

00:06:59.750 --> 00:07:00.689
It drives me nuts.

00:07:00.689 --> 00:07:02.605
I do not want to be above average.

00:07:02.605 --> 00:07:04.868
I want you guys to hold me
to a higher standard too.

00:07:04.868 --> 00:07:07.501
I want suggestions on how
to make things better.

00:07:07.501 --> 00:07:09.559
But when I look at the things that I make,

00:07:09.559 --> 00:07:11.773
I'm equally happy with
them, like I'm proud

00:07:11.773 --> 00:07:13.436
of what we made with the
resources that we had,

00:07:13.436 --> 00:07:14.557
the skills, ability.

00:07:14.557 --> 00:07:16.194
But at the same time,
I want it to be better.

00:07:16.194 --> 00:07:19.422
I want it to be, I want it to be more.

00:07:19.422 --> 00:07:20.716
This is what we do.

00:07:20.716 --> 00:07:23.011
Progress equals happiness,
you want to grow,

00:07:23.011 --> 00:07:24.271
you want to continue to get better.

00:07:24.271 --> 00:07:25.891
Otherwise you get bored.

00:07:25.891 --> 00:07:28.474
And your customers get bored,
your audience gets bored.

00:07:28.474 --> 00:07:31.153
And so I don't think
you should ever settle

00:07:31.153 --> 00:07:32.449
for above average in anything.

00:07:32.449 --> 00:07:34.347
If you know you can do
better, if you're performing

00:07:34.347 --> 00:07:36.483
at the top of you abilities right now,

00:07:36.483 --> 00:07:38.161
then that's okay, that's great.

00:07:38.161 --> 00:07:39.265
That's what you want to be doing.

00:07:39.265 --> 00:07:40.881
But if you know you can do better,

00:07:40.881 --> 00:07:42.466
you got to go push harder.

00:07:42.466 --> 00:07:44.503
You know, there's a lot
of people who may look up

00:07:44.503 --> 00:07:46.869
to somebody and say well
look at what they're doing.

00:07:46.869 --> 00:07:49.326
And you know you can get there
but you're not there yet.

00:07:49.326 --> 00:07:51.422
You want to play this
beautiful piece of piano.

00:07:51.422 --> 00:07:52.336
You know you can get there and

00:07:52.336 --> 00:07:55.310
you're just starting off
learning a couple keys.

00:07:55.310 --> 00:07:57.283
Maybe right now, that's all
you can do is a couple keys.

00:07:57.283 --> 00:07:59.782
But you can work harder
to get better and improve,

00:07:59.782 --> 00:08:02.435
improve, improve, improve, improve.

00:08:02.435 --> 00:08:04.764
Progress equals happiness.

00:08:04.764 --> 00:08:06.713
Stop settling for average.

00:08:06.713 --> 00:08:07.576
And you know what?

00:08:07.576 --> 00:08:09.553
One thing I would challenge you to do,

00:08:09.553 --> 00:08:13.369
it's always easy to lean in on empathy

00:08:13.369 --> 00:08:15.913
when you see a friend who's down.

00:08:15.913 --> 00:08:18.184
It's easy to lean in on empathy.

00:08:18.184 --> 00:08:20.570
But maybe you should
push them to do better.

00:08:20.570 --> 00:08:22.639
Even when somebody's down on their luck.

00:08:22.639 --> 00:08:25.669
Or maybe somebody made a
video and they sucked at it.

00:08:25.669 --> 00:08:29.681
Maybe telling them, I
feel you, I know you can

00:08:29.681 --> 00:08:31.127
do a lot better.

00:08:31.127 --> 00:08:32.796
Instead of just saying,
that was really good.

00:08:32.796 --> 00:08:34.726
When you know that it
wasn't even really good,

00:08:34.726 --> 00:08:37.153
right, we tell ourselves
and we tell others

00:08:37.153 --> 00:08:38.873
that things that something is really good

00:08:38.873 --> 00:08:40.324
when we know it's not.

00:08:40.324 --> 00:08:41.711
And you don't have to beat them down,

00:08:41.711 --> 00:08:44.517
but telling them that you
know they can do better,

00:08:44.517 --> 00:08:46.501
you believe in them, can
make all the difference

00:08:46.501 --> 00:08:48.028
in the world in bringing them back up and

00:08:48.028 --> 00:08:51.615
shooting beyond their comfort zone.

00:08:51.615 --> 00:08:53.411
Stop settling for average.

00:08:53.411 --> 00:08:54.968
So the question of the day today is

00:08:54.968 --> 00:08:57.396
I'm curious, what are you guys right now

00:08:57.396 --> 00:09:00.046
settling for average in
that you want to start

00:09:00.046 --> 00:09:01.546
pushing harder on?

00:09:02.445 --> 00:09:03.869
Leave it down in the comments below.

00:09:03.869 --> 00:09:05.581
I'm curious to see what
you guys have to say.

00:09:05.581 --> 00:09:07.264
I also want to give a
quick shout out to Milica

00:09:07.264 --> 00:09:08.946
I hope I pronounced that
okay, thank you so much

00:09:08.946 --> 00:09:11.244
for bringing up a copy of my book.

00:09:11.244 --> 00:09:13.602
Your one word really really
really means a lot to me and

00:09:13.602 --> 00:09:15.466
I hope you're enjoying the read.

00:09:15.466 --> 00:09:16.720
Thank you guys again for watching.

00:09:16.720 --> 00:09:17.783
I believe in you.

00:09:17.783 --> 00:09:19.743
I hope you continue to
believe in yourself and

00:09:19.743 --> 00:09:21.994
whatever your one word is.

00:09:21.994 --> 00:09:24.516
Much love and I'll see
you again tomorrow morning

00:09:24.516 --> 00:09:26.933
for another Shot of Espresso.

00:09:28.124 --> 00:09:31.057
♫ I wake up every morning

00:09:31.057 --> 00:09:34.474
♫ Espresso keep me going

00:09:37.566 --> 00:09:39.753
- I mean when I was 22,
right after I graduated

00:09:39.753 --> 00:09:42.299
from Dartmouth, I was so focused on making

00:09:42.299 --> 00:09:47.107
everyone happy that I almost
chose the worst possible

00:09:47.107 --> 00:09:48.634
career for my personality.

00:09:48.634 --> 00:09:50.812
It's not a bad career, it just
would have been horrendous

00:09:50.812 --> 00:09:51.800
for me.

00:09:51.800 --> 00:09:54.911
I was interested in the
environment so I decided,

00:09:54.911 --> 00:09:56.935
oh you know, I'll go get a law degree and

00:09:56.935 --> 00:09:58.607
then I'll go work in Washington.

00:09:58.607 --> 00:10:01.000
And I think maybe I'll work
on environmental policy and

00:10:01.000 --> 00:10:03.365
I'd probably end up in some cube farm.

00:10:03.365 --> 00:10:05.924
And everyone was thrilled with the plan.

00:10:05.924 --> 00:10:08.711
Everyone, it turns out, but me.

00:10:08.711 --> 00:10:11.774
So here I am, I'm driving
a Uhaul across country

00:10:11.774 --> 00:10:13.800
to go to law school and to get a degree

00:10:13.800 --> 00:10:15.316
in environmental law.

00:10:15.316 --> 00:10:18.316
And something started to gnaw at me.

00:10:19.251 --> 00:10:23.092
And with every single mile that I drove,

00:10:23.092 --> 00:10:25.722
my thoughts were getting louder.

00:10:25.722 --> 00:10:27.840
And doubts were starting to pour in.

00:10:27.840 --> 00:10:32.403
My gut was telling me, Mel,
turn the damn Uhaul around.

00:10:32.403 --> 00:10:34.374
But the problem was that
everything was already

00:10:34.374 --> 00:10:35.477
in place, right?

00:10:35.477 --> 00:10:37.402
I mean I'm already in the Uhaul,

00:10:37.402 --> 00:10:39.572
the thing is already packed.

00:10:39.572 --> 00:10:41.779
I'm already 10 miles into my drive.

00:10:41.779 --> 00:10:43.825
The tuition had been paid
for the first semester.

00:10:43.825 --> 00:10:45.665
I had signed a lease.

00:10:45.665 --> 00:10:48.785
I mean I could not undo these things.

00:10:48.785 --> 00:10:52.209
Isn't that why it's so difficult for you

00:10:52.209 --> 00:10:54.307
to make changes in your life?

00:10:54.307 --> 00:10:57.594
Because you think that
things can't be undone.

00:10:57.594 --> 00:10:59.888
The fact is, any excuse
that you come up with,

00:10:59.888 --> 00:11:00.914
you can undo.

00:11:00.914 --> 00:11:02.535
Tuition can be reimbursed.

00:11:02.535 --> 00:11:03.962
Apartments can be leased.

00:11:03.962 --> 00:11:05.674
Plan B can be invented.

00:11:05.674 --> 00:11:09.912
So I got up, I repacked the
Uhaul and I drove out of town.

00:11:09.912 --> 00:11:13.035
I let myself make a u-turn in life.

00:11:13.035 --> 00:11:15.654
If you ever find your
gut battling your head,

00:11:15.654 --> 00:11:17.390
save yourself the drama.

00:11:17.390 --> 00:11:19.936
I guarantee you, your gut is right.

00:11:19.936 --> 00:11:23.099
I guarantee you, your
excuses can be undone.

00:11:23.099 --> 00:11:26.652
And I guarantee you, you can
make a u-turn in your life

00:11:26.652 --> 00:11:28.672
right now if you want to.

00:11:28.672 --> 00:11:32.442
So if it were easy to get
what you wanted in life,

00:11:32.442 --> 00:11:34.305
Google would have already
figured out an app.

00:11:34.305 --> 00:11:37.279
You would just type in,
okay I'm a student and

00:11:37.279 --> 00:11:39.547
I want to go from being a
student to being successful.

00:11:39.547 --> 00:11:41.088
And Google would tell you, go to college,

00:11:41.088 --> 00:11:45.195
then you get your Masters,
then you land this killer job.

00:11:45.195 --> 00:11:47.661
And then you put in a bunch
of face time while you're

00:11:47.661 --> 00:11:49.168
checking Facebook.

00:11:49.168 --> 00:11:51.181
Then you get promoted to
manager and then you realize

00:11:51.181 --> 00:11:52.941
managing people kind of stinks.

00:11:52.941 --> 00:11:55.075
And then you keep climbing
the corporate ladder.

00:11:55.075 --> 00:11:58.099
And then you start to wonder,
well how did I end up here?

00:11:58.099 --> 00:11:59.732
And then you go, is this
what success looks like,

00:11:59.732 --> 00:12:01.420
you're like, no, I'm go to J. Hilburn.

00:12:01.420 --> 00:12:03.150
That's what success looks like.

00:12:03.150 --> 00:12:05.400
(applause)

00:12:06.570 --> 00:12:09.291
So keep this in mind, if
there's something that you want,

00:12:09.291 --> 00:12:12.076
like seven people, or a trip to Africa,

00:12:12.076 --> 00:12:14.059
or you're going to make it to Mexico,

00:12:14.059 --> 00:12:16.545
in the pink shirt, I'm
looking at you again, sorry.

00:12:16.545 --> 00:12:17.962
I'm watching you.

00:12:19.235 --> 00:12:21.035
And rooting for you.

00:12:21.035 --> 00:12:22.883
Keep in mind this.

00:12:22.883 --> 00:12:25.555
Here you are, this is what you want.

00:12:25.555 --> 00:12:27.702
I spend a lot of time on lacrosse fields.

00:12:27.702 --> 00:12:29.128
Although they don't really look like this.

00:12:29.128 --> 00:12:32.230
You tend to think that what you want,

00:12:32.230 --> 00:12:34.180
you just march right towards it.

00:12:34.180 --> 00:12:37.534
But if in sports, you march
right towards the goal,

00:12:37.534 --> 00:12:38.610
what happens?

00:12:38.610 --> 00:12:39.944
The defenders come in.

00:12:39.944 --> 00:12:42.276
And what the defenders
are is your brain saying

00:12:42.276 --> 00:12:43.843
ain't going to happen.

00:12:43.843 --> 00:12:46.114
So the second you start moving
toward that thing you want,

00:12:46.114 --> 00:12:47.244
be ready.

00:12:47.244 --> 00:12:48.697
You're going to tell yourself
you don't feel like it.

00:12:48.697 --> 00:12:50.987
You're going to have to force
yourself, it's happening.

00:12:50.987 --> 00:12:52.940
There's no way to get around it.

00:12:52.940 --> 00:12:54.274
So what you're going to have to do is

00:12:54.274 --> 00:12:58.454
you're going to basically
get bounced around a lot.

00:12:58.454 --> 00:13:00.003
All over the place.

00:13:00.003 --> 00:13:01.260
And there are going to be a lot of times

00:13:01.260 --> 00:13:03.188
that you feel like, this
was a really dumb idea

00:13:03.188 --> 00:13:07.185
to start this business,
because it's going to get hard.

00:13:07.185 --> 00:13:09.972
And I want to remind you about something.

00:13:09.972 --> 00:13:13.215
Unlike a sports field where
there is an in and out

00:13:13.215 --> 00:13:15.765
of bounds, the great thing about life is

00:13:15.765 --> 00:13:17.907
there actually aren't any.

00:13:17.907 --> 00:13:20.099
And it's usually in those
moments where you feel

00:13:20.099 --> 00:13:24.299
like you can't do it, that
you're closer than ever

00:13:24.299 --> 00:13:26.794
to having everything that you wanted.

00:13:26.794 --> 00:13:29.393
And I wanted to show you this
so that you keep it in mind

00:13:29.393 --> 00:13:32.346
because I think a lot of
times when you look back,

00:13:32.346 --> 00:13:34.795
it's the darkest moments where you realize

00:13:34.795 --> 00:13:37.362
holy cow, that's what
projected me forward.

